            :cost-efficiency 0.76
            :dependency-independence 0.85}}
  {:id "us-no-pe"
   :label "US corporation imports and sells while asserting no Japan PE"
   :tax-model :us-corporation-no-japan-pe
   :assumptions
   ["The US corporation has no Japanese fixed place, dependent contract agent, or non-auxiliary activity creating a PE."
    "Japanese warehousing and delivery are performed by an independent provider within treaty limits."
    "The US corporation appoints the required Japanese customs and tax agents and completes Japanese consumption-tax obligations."
    "The US state corporate income-tax rate is zero in the illustrative model; this is not an observed fact."]
   :outcomes
   ["Potential 21% US federal corporate rate before state tax while profits remain in the corporation."
    "Japanese consumption tax and import administration remain."
    "PE, state nexus, shareholder extraction, and dual-country compliance can eliminate the apparent rate advantage."]
   :scores {:expected-value 0.58
            :evidence-confidence 0.45
            :reversibility 0.55
            :authority-fit 0.35
            :time-efficiency 0.35
            :cost-efficiency 0.60
            :dependency-independence 0.30}}
  {:id "split-hardware-ip"
   :label "Japanese hardware distributor with separately governed US IP or cloud economics"
   :tax-model :split-not-computed
   :assumptions
   ["The Japanese corporation imports, sells, invoices, and supports hardware."
    "Any US charge for IP, cloud, or service is commercially real, separately evidenced, treaty-reviewed, and arm's-length."
    "Related-party allocation is not used to move an arbitrary residual profit."]
   :outcomes
   ["Local hardware operations remain simple while a real US IP or cloud function can retain its supported economics."
    "Transfer pricing, withholding classification, and treaty eligibility require professional review before execution."
    "No numeric income-tax advantage is claimed until the intercompany allocation and actual functions are known."]
   :scores {:expected-value 0.78
            :evidence-confidence 0.58
            :reversibility 0.58
            :authority-fit 0.62
            :time-efficiency 0.50
            :cost-efficiency 0.65
            :dependency-independence 0.45}}]

 :selected "jp-direct"
 :selection-rationale
 "For a Japan-operated launch at the current evidence level, the Japanese corporation route has the strongest evidence, authority fit, and execution efficiency. The US no-PE route is a conditional scale option, not the default. The split route remains a later design option only if Murakumo IP/cloud functions and arm's-length pricing are real and documented."

